id: design.timeout-budget
kind: design
title: timeout budget propagation
aliases: timeout budget, deadline propagation, remaining budget
tags: design, timeouts, resilience
questions:
  - how much time should a downstream call get?
  - how do you avoid timeout storms at the edge of a request?
invariant: Each downstream hop receives a slice of the caller's remaining budget, never more, so timeouts concentrate near the leaf that actually stalls.
answer_30s: Compute the child timeout as remaining = deadline - now, and pass the deadline (not a fresh timeout) to children so the subtraction is exact at each hop; at the edge, shed load instead of borrowing against a budget you do not have.
when_to_use:
  - request handlers that fan out to multiple downstream calls
  - any client of a service that takes a deadline
related:
  - design.cascading-timeouts
  - design.timeouts
  - design.load-shedding
sources:
  - https://sre.google/sre-book/request-latency/
